    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43790" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septŭāginta</span></b> , num. adj.
		for septumaginta, septem-decenta, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>seventy</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. Arb.
				4, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centum septuaginta,</span>”
				<i>a hundred and seventy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 52, § 121</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septuaginta et tres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					35, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septem et septuaginta annos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Att. 21, 1</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">with numerals: interficiuntur IV. et LXX.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 4, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
